From a3ef7cc381020bc5f8525cfc5b903bec3373cc36 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Junction 2026 team <junction2026@localhost>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:56:41 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 01/13] feat(backend): capture RealSense color, aligned depth
 or both

The RealSense payload's output_type and depth range were dropped by the camera
factory, and physicalai's RealSenseCamera always streams depth at the color
resolution (1920x1080 fails with "Couldn't resolve requests") while its
publisher forwards color only.

Studio now captures RealSense cameras with its own RealSenseRGBDCamera: it
enables only the streams output_type asks for, aligns depth to color, and
packs color and depth of one frameset into a single uint8 frame so they share
a timestamp through the unchanged shared-memory publisher. The requested mode
is checked against the modes the device offers on its current USB connection,
with a clear error (including a USB 2 hint) when it is not available. Each
output type gets its own publisher service. The supported-formats endpoint
lists the modes per output type and is no longer cached for RealSense, and a
preview shows color, or colorized depth for depth-only cameras.

The portable runtime-export recipe now gives physicalai's RealSenseCamera a
depth resolution the D400 depth sensor has.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
